---
// The desktop "On this page" rail — one definition, four pages.
//
// EXTRACTED 2026-08-05. The rail existed as page-local copies on the [slug]
// lesson template and on /learn/rules; giving it to /learn/ladder and
// /learn/bitcoin-keys (backlog 16c) would have made FOUR copies of one thing,
// which is this project's most-repeated bug shape applied to CSS. The copies
// had already drifted in small ways nobody would ever have noticed, because a
// rail that looks slightly different on one page reads as a design choice.
//
// THE GRID LIVES HERE TOO, and it has to be `is:global`. The two-column layout
// is a property of the PAGE's wrapper (`.lgrid`), an element this component does
// not render — and an Astro scoped rule compiles to `.lgrid[data-astro-cid-<this
// file>]`, which matches nothing. That is the silent-scoped-style failure already
// registered in the spine; it is silent precisely because the page still renders,
// just in one column. Verify a new rail by loading the page at ≥1200px and
// confirming there are two columns, never by reading the diff.
//
// Desktop only, by design: it fills the empty right canvas on wide screens and
// phones never see it. Static anchor list, no scroll-spy — a rail that tracks
// scroll position is a behaviour to maintain, and this one only has to be a map.
//
// PROPS
//   items    [{ id, label, n? }]  — `n` renders a monospace number before the
//                                   label (the /learn/rules variant)
//   label    the rail's own heading; defaults to "On this page"
//   min      hide the rail below this many items (default 3) — a two-entry
//            table of contents is furniture, not navigation
const { items = [], label = 'On this page', min = 3 } = Astro.props;
const show = items.length >= min;
---
{show && (
  <aside class="toc" aria-label={label}>
    <p class="toc-k mono">{label}</p>
    <ol>
      {items.map((t) => (
        <li>
          <a href={`#${t.id}`}>
            {t.n != null && <span class="toc-n mono">{t.n}</span>}
            {t.label}
          </a>
        </li>
      ))}
    </ol>
  </aside>
)}

<style is:global>
  /* `.lgrid` is the PAGE's wrapper, not this component's — see the header note
     on why these rules cannot be scoped. */
  .toc { display: none; }
  @media (min-width: 1200px) {
    .lgrid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 15rem; gap: 3.5rem; align-items: start; }
    .toc { display: block; position: sticky; top: 5.5rem; max-height: calc(100vh - 7rem);
      overflow-y: auto; border-left: 1px solid var(--line-soft); padding-left: 1.25rem; }
    .toc-k { font-size: 0.78rem; letter-spacing: 0.14em; text-transform: uppercase;
      color: var(--faint); font-weight: 600; margin: 0 0 0.7rem; }
    .toc ol { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.55rem; }
    .toc a { display: block; color: var(--muted); font-size: 0.86rem; line-height: 1.4; text-decoration: none; }
    .toc a:hover { color: var(--accent); }
    .toc-n { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; font-size: 0.78rem; margin-right: 0.45rem; }
  }
</style>
